  "activity": {
    "id": "act_vsepr_training",
    "name": "Predicting Molecular Geometry with VSEPR Theory",
    "description": "A hands-on AR training that guides General Chemistry I students through VSEPR theory: counting electron domains, watching the minimum-repulsion principle produce the five electron-domain geometries, distinguishing electron-domain from molecular geometry, understanding lone-pair angular asymmetry, and applying predictions to real molecules through two interactive challenges.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_vsepr_lab",
    "start": "act_intro",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "act_intro",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_central_stage",
        "predicate": "pred_intro_narration",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1. The Core Idea of VSEPR",
          "description": "Meet the central atom, glowing at the center of your workspace. VSEPR theory says the electron pairs around it \u2014 both bonding pairs and lone pairs \u2014 repel each other and spread out as far apart as possible. Check the reference panel to your side: it shows a flat Lewis structure of water and reminds you that each single, double, or triple bond, and each lone pair, counts as ONE electron domain. Say or tap 'Next' to begin."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_central_atom_glow",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_lewis_card",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_lewis_water_image",
              "poi": "poi_card_face"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_central_stage",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_intro_narration"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_geometry",
              "poi": "poi_axial_top",
              "text": "Central Atom"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_lewis_card",
              "type": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_geometry",
              "poi": "poi_axial_top"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_central_stage",
              "type": "predicate"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "act_minrepulsion",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "act_minrepulsion",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_minrepulsion",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_central_stage",
        "predicate": "pred_narration_scene",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2. Minimum Repulsion in Action",
          "description": "Watch two lobed electron-domain clouds drift apart until they sit 180\u00b0 apart \u2014 a LINEAR arrangement. A third domain joins and they rearrange to TRIGONAL PLANAR at 120\u00b0. A fourth produces a TETRAHEDRON at 109.5\u00b0. Notice the faint repulsion vectors flash between domains as they push apart, then fade as the shape stabilizes. Tap 'Next' to complete the catalog."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_electron_domains",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_domain_repulsion_anim",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_electron_domains",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_repulsion_vectors",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_geometry_linear",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_central_stage",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_scene"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_geometry",
              "poi": "poi_axial_top",
              "text": "Linear 180 -> Trigonal Planar 120 -> Tetrahedral 109.5"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_electron_domains",
              "type": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "augmentation": "pred_geometry_linear"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_geometry",
              "poi": "poi_axial_top"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_central_stage",
              "type": "predicate"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "act_full_catalog",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "act_full_catalog",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "act_full_catalog",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_central_stage",
        "predicate": "pred_narration_scene",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3. Completing the Five Geometries",
          "description": "Building from the tetrahedron, a fifth domain arranges into TRIGONAL BIPYRAMIDAL \u2014 three equatorial domains at 120\u00b0 plus two axial domains at 90\u00b0. A sixth produces an OCTAHEDRAL arrangement with every neighbor at 90\u00b0. Rotate the molecule freely to view it from any angle. The summary panel shows all five electron-domain geometries with their domain counts (2, 3, 4, 5, 6) and angles (180\u00b0, 120\u00b0, 109.5\u00b0, 90\u00b0/120\u00b0, 90\u00b0). Tap 'Next'."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_geometry_trigonal_bipyramidal",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_central_atom",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_geometry_octahedral",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_summary_panel",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_geometry_summary_panel",
              "poi": "poi_panel_face"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_central_stage",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_scene"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
